The manifold's surface carries texture across the entire scene area — no empty background — since the curvature must also be visible through its distortion. Landmarks are heterogeneous and asymmetrically arranged; a single repeating primitive (stripes, dots, a grid) as the entire visual content of a scene is not allowed.
- In scenes with non-trivial topology: if a single landmark is visible simultaneously from multiple directions, all its visible images are rendered from one and the same 4D object instance via different identification paths. Check: modifying the object synchronously changes all of its images.

## 5. Controls and Architecture

A main menu with scene selection and a way to return to it. Free real-time flight through the manifold. HTML as the entry point, with JS/shaders/scene data in separate files. No mandatory build step; if a build step exists, include run instructions.